---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
const baseUrl = (import.meta.env.BASE_URL || '/').replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Layout lang="en" title="OmniPrep — A Unified Pipeline for Accelerating Large-Scale Multimodal MRI Research" description="OmniPrep — unified multimodal MRI preprocessing and analysis pipeline." active="home">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="hero-badge"><span class="dot"></span> Multi-modal · Scalable · Reproducible</span>
        <h1>A Unified Pipeline for <span class="grad">Accelerating</span> <span class="grad grad-2">Large-Scale Multimodal MRI Research</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
            OmniPrep unifies sMRI, dMRI, and fMRI preprocessing and downstream analysis, from atlas-based ROI features to connectomics, accelerated by deep learning and parallel computing.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${baseUrl}/getting-started/`}>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/></svg>
            Get Started
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${baseUrl}/docs/`}>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 016.5 17H20"/><path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 014 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 016.5 2z"/></svg>
            Read the Docs
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-terminal">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <span class="tdot r"></span><span class="tdot y"></span><span class="tdot g"></span>
            <span class="terminal-title">bash — omniprep</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <span class="p">$</span> <span class="k">docker run</span> <span class="o">-it --rm --gpus all</span><span class="cont">\</span><br />
            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="o">-v /path/to/bids:/data -v /path/to/output:/out</span><span class="cont">\</span><br />
            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="o">-v /path/to/license.txt:/license.txt</span><span class="cont">\</span><br />
            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="s">uxhao/omniprep:latest</span> <span class="o">/data /out participant</span><span class="cont">\</span><br />
            &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="o">--fs_license_file /license.txt</span> <span class="o">--tasks</span> <span class="s">"anat bold dwi"</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROBLEMS -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">The real-world problem</span>
          <h2>What OmniPrep solves</h2>
          <p class="lead">Large-scale brain imaging now combines sMRI, fMRI and dMRI at cohort scale. Turning raw data into analyzable features has become the first bottleneck — for four concrete reasons.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-2">
          <div class="card problem-card">
            <span class="tag">Problem 01</span>
            <h3>Fragmented multimodal workflows</h3>
            <p>Structural, functional and diffusion processing still rely on FreeSurfer, fMRIPrep and dMRIPrep as separate tools with incompatible interfaces and outputs. Gluing them together takes hand-written scripts, and results across modalities are hard to compare.</p>
            <div class="solve">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
              <span><strong>Solved</strong> — all three modalities run in one workflow, with inter-modality dependencies scheduled automatically.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card problem-card">
            <span class="tag">Problem 02</span>
            <h3>Too slow at cohort scale</h3>
            <p>Mainstream pipelines are designed for serial execution on a single machine, without parallel scheduling or deep-learning acceleration. Preprocessing a thousand-subject cohort takes months, and a mid-run failure is costly to recover from.</p>
            <div class="solve">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
              <span><strong>Solved</strong> — deep-learning models for key reconstruction steps, Nextflow task-level parallelism, and VELA-GPU elastic scheduling with checkpoint resume.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card problem-card">
            <span class="tag">Problem 03</span>
            <h3>Incomplete lifespan coverage</h3>
            <p>Templates and distortion-correction strategies are split between adult, pediatric and infant cohorts, so cross-age studies require heavy manual adaptation. Quality control still depends on visual inspection, with no QC built into the pipeline.</p>
            <div class="solve">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
              <span><strong>Solved</strong> — automatic age detection with matching MNI templates and distortion strategies, plus automated QC reports on every run.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card problem-card">
            <span class="tag">Problem 04</span>
            <h3>Stops at preprocessing, and hard to use</h3>
            <p>Most pipelines stop at preprocessing: morphometric features, time series and connectomes still have to be computed separately. They also demand real engineering skill, so clinical researchers without a technical background cannot run the full chain.</p>
            <div class="solve">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6L9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
              <span><strong>Solved</strong> — analysis-ready features are produced end to end, and the whole chain runs from a single container command with no coding.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- INNOVATIONS -->
    <section class="section soft">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Key innovations</span>
          <h2>Six innovations, one continuous chain</h2>
          <p class="lead">From raw data to conclusions: unified · accelerated · lifespan-wide · end-to-end · reproducible · zero-code.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-3">
          <div class="card innovation-card">
            <span class="idx">01</span>
            <span class="en">Unified</span>
            <h3>Unified multimodal workflow</h3>
            <p>Structural, functional and diffusion modalities are preprocessed and analyzed within a single workflow, with inter-modality dependencies scheduled automatically — no stitching independent tools together.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card innovation-card featured">
            <span class="idx">02</span>
            <span class="en">Accelerating</span>
            <h3>Deep learning &amp; parallel acceleration</h3>
            <p>Deep-learning models accelerate key reconstruction steps, combined with Nextflow task-level parallelism and our in-house VELA-GPU elastic memory scheduler — large cohorts no longer take months.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card innovation-card">
            <span class="idx">03</span>
            <span class="en">Across the Lifespan</span>
            <h3>Lifespan coverage</h3>
            <p>Adult, pediatric and infant cohorts are age-detected automatically, then matched to the corresponding MNI templates and distortion-correction strategies — one pipeline for every age range.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card innovation-card">
            <span class="idx">04</span>
            <span class="en">End-to-end</span>
            <h3>Analysis-ready features</h3>
            <p>More than preprocessing: morphometry, ROI time series, FC, ReHo/ALFF, structural connectomes and CIFTI outputs — features that feed directly into group-level statistics.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card innovation-card">
            <span class="idx">05</span>
            <span class="en">Reproducible</span>
            <h3>Built-in QC &amp; reproducibility</h3>
            <p>Automated QC reports, motion scrubbing and FD-based frame detection come with every run; locked container versions and traceable <code style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">trace</code> make results reproducible and trustworthy.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card innovation-card">
            <span class="idx">06</span>
            <span class="en">Zero-code</span>
            <h3>Zero-code entry point</h3>
            <p>Engineering complexity stays inside the container and workflow. Users face a single command, so clinical researchers can run the full chain independently without programming.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STATS -->
    <section class="stats">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">3</div>
          <div class="stat-label">MRI modalities</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">6<span class="unit">+</span></div>
          <div class="stat-label">Built-in atlases</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">60<span class="unit">+</span></div>
          <div class="stat-label">Configuration options</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-num">2</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Container runtimes</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- MODALITIES -->
    <section class="section soft">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Three modalities, one pipeline</span>
          <h2>End-to-end multimodal workflows</h2>
          <p class="lead">Enable the tasks you need with the <code style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">--tasks</code> flag — dependencies between modalities are handled automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="modality">
          <div class="modality-card anat">
            <span class="modality-badge">anat</span>
            <h3>Structural MRI</h3>
            <div class="sub">T1w preprocessing &amp; reconstruction</div>
            <p>FreeSurfer-based cortical reconstruction and segmentation, producing surfaces, parcellations, and atlas-level morphometric features.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>FreeSurfer reconstruction</li>
              <li>ROI-level morphometry</li>
              <li>Native &amp; MNI-space surfaces</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="more" href={`${baseUrl}/docs/#general-options`}>Learn more →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="modality-card bold">
            <span class="modality-badge">bold</span>
            <h3>Functional MRI</h3>
            <div class="sub">BOLD preprocessing &amp; derivatives</div>
            <p>Full BOLD denoising chain with motion scrubbing, nuisance regression, temporal filtering, and a rich set of voxel- and ROI-level metrics.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>ReHo, ALFF/fALFF, INT</li>
              <li>ROI time series &amp; FC matrices</li>
              <li>CIFTI &amp; surface outputs</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="more" href={`${baseUrl}/docs/#bold-options`}>Learn more →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="modality-card dwi">
            <span class="modality-badge">dwi</span>
            <h3>Diffusion MRI</h3>
            <div class="sub">DWI preprocessing, tractography &amp; connectomics</div>
            <p>Distortion correction, DTI and CSD metrics, whole-brain tractography (iFOD2, SD-Stream, tensor), and structural connectomes.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>DTI &amp; CSD metrics</li>
              <li>Whole-brain tractography</li>
              <li>Structural connectomes</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="more" href={`${baseUrl}/docs/#dwi-options`}>Learn more →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- QUICK START -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Quick start</span>
          <h2>Run in three steps</h2>
          <p class="lead">From raw BIDS data to derivatives in minutes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-2" style="align-items:start">
          <div>
            <ol class="steps">
              <li>
                <h4>Pull the container image</h4>
                <p>Get the pre-built OmniPrep image from Docker Hub.</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                  <div class="cb-head"><span class="cb-label">bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
                  <pre><code>docker pull uxhao/omniprep:latest</code></pre>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <h4>Prepare your BIDS dataset &amp; license</h4>
                <p>Point OmniPrep at your BIDS directory and a FreeSurfer license file.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <h4>Launch the pipeline</h4>
                <p>Run the workflow with the modalities you need.</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                  <div class="cb-head"><span class="cb-label">bash</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
                  <pre><code>docker run -it --rm --gpus all \
  -v /path/to/bids:/data \
  -v /path/to/output:/out \
  -v /path/to/license.txt:/license.txt \
  uxhao/omniprep:latest /data /out participant \
  --fs_license_file /license.txt \
  --tasks "anat bold dwi"</code></pre>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="card" style="box-shadow:var(--shadow-md)">
              <h3 style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px">
                <span class="card-icon green" style="margin:0;width:34px;height:34px"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 11-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg></span>
                What you get
              </h3>
              <p>OmniPrep writes a BIDS-derivatives-compatible tree under <code style="font-family:var(--font-mono)">output_dir/derivatives/omniprep</code>, including:</p>
              <div class="pill-row">
                <span class="pill hl">Recon/</span>
                <span class="pill hl">BOLD/</span>
                <span class="pill hl">DWI/</span>
                <span class="pill hl">QC/</span>
                <span class="pill">report.html</span>
                <span class="pill">timeline.html</span>
              </div>
              <ul style="margin-top:16px;padding-left:20px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">
                <li>FreeSurfer reconstruction &amp; morphometry</li>
                <li>Denoised BOLD + voxel/ROI metrics</li>
                <li>Tractography &amp; connectomes</li>
                <li>Automated QC reports</li>
              </ul>
              <a class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:16px" href={`${baseUrl}/getting-started/`}>View full guide →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="section soft">
      <div class="container" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px">
        <h2>Ready to preprocess at scale?</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:28px">
          Read the documentation to explore every option, or jump straight into installation.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={`${baseUrl}/docs/`}>Browse Documentation</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${baseUrl}/about/`}>About the Project</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  
</Layout>
